WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.484
Secure file upload handling in ASP.

2
00:00:02.484 --> 00:00:05.750
NET Core is a repeatable engineering workflow.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:14.693
Start by identifying every upload entry point, including forms, APIs, imports, partner integrations, and administrative tools.

4
00:00:14.693 --> 00:00:21.721
Apply request, form, multipart, endpoint, file count, and business limits that match each workflow.

5
00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:25.980
Treat file names, paths, metadata, and content as untrusted.

6
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:38.969
Generate internal storage identifiers, keep client names as display metadata when needed, avoid client-controlled paths, and store uploaded files outside executable application roots.

7
00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:44.577
Separate temporary, quarantined, private, public, and processed storage states.

8
00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:49.759
Validate file categories using business allow-lists and multiple signals.

9
00:00:49.759 --> 00:01:01.542
Extensions, MIME types, signatures, metadata, structure, size, and processing expectations all provide useful information, but no single signal proves a file is safe.

10
00:01:01.542 --> 00:01:08.995
Accepted files may still need quarantine, scanning, review, or asynchronous processing before normal use.

11
00:01:08.995 --> 00:01:12.544
Enforce authorization on both upload and download.

12
00:01:12.544 --> 00:01:19.500
Check purpose, tenant, ownership, role, and object-level access before accepting or serving files.

13
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:31.283
Avoid exposing internal storage paths and make sure thumbnails, previews, processed derivatives, and temporary links do not bypass the rules for the original content.

14
00:01:31.283 --> 00:01:33.413
Finally, operate the pipeline.

15
00:01:33.413 --> 00:01:48.461
Log useful state transitions without storing sensitive contents, monitor unusual patterns and processing failures, review dependencies and storage permissions, protect secrets, and maintain cleanup and retention.

16
00:01:48.461 --> 00:01:54.282
A safer upload system is one the team can explain, monitor, and improve over time.
